From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0041] map shared memories as private ones and grow them the same way

A shared memory reserved its whole maximum up front. It now maps and grows
as a private memory does, extending or moving its map when growth passes it,
which is safe because it grows only while no parallel call runs: the host
freezes it for the length of each call and a frozen memory refuses to grow.
Compiled code reloads a shared memory's base at the same points as a private
one's.

